WEBVTT

00:00:00.407 --> 00:00:09.643
In this video, you will see Event Partner, the plan for cities, chambers of commerce, nonprofits and event producers that run several events in a season.

00:00:09.643 --> 00:00:14.866
You will see what it is, how an organization gets it, and how you use it on your events.

00:00:14.866 --> 00:00:15.839
We start on the map.

00:00:16.809 --> 00:00:18.483
Start at SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:21.291 --> 00:00:23.841
On the home page, tap Use my location.

00:00:25.495 --> 00:00:26.475
Then tap Allow.

00:00:29.918 --> 00:00:33.366
Look at the top right corner of the map, and tap the three dots.

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:37.964
In the menu, tap Promote your event.

00:00:39.742 --> 00:00:42.203
Listing an event is always free.

00:00:42.203 --> 00:00:45.310
This is for organizers who want to stand out.

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:47.479
This page features one event.

00:00:47.479 --> 00:00:54.608
Look at the sentence at the top: Run several events a season as a city, chamber, nonprofit or event producer?

00:00:54.608 --> 00:00:55.712
See Event Partner.

00:00:56.475 --> 00:00:57.672
Tap Event Partner.

00:00:59.684 --> 00:01:01.980
This is the Event Partner page.

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:06.093
It is for an organization that runs several events in a season.

00:01:06.093 --> 00:01:09.730
One payment covers up to ten of your events for the season.

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:15.551
Each covered event gets the gold Featured pin on the map, and an Event Partner badge on its page.

00:01:16.307 --> 00:01:19.090
Listing an event stays free for everyone.

00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:22.361
Event Partner is only for events you want to stand out.

00:01:22.361 --> 00:01:26.864
The price is on the card, and you pay once for the season, with no subscription.

00:01:27.624 --> 00:01:29.523
To buy it, you tap Pay on Stripe.

00:01:31.482 --> 00:01:34.280
That opens Stripe's secure payment page.

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:40.213
We stop here, because this is only a demonstration, and we never enter card details in a video.

00:01:41.069 --> 00:01:43.920
After you pay, the page shows your plan.

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:50.129
It counts how many of your ten events you have used this season, and lists the events it already covers.

00:01:50.129 --> 00:01:53.200
Under Choose an event are your other live events.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:56.351
Tap Use the plan next to the event you want to cover.

00:01:58.323 --> 00:02:03.829
The page says the event is Featured through its last day, and the count goes up by one.

00:02:03.829 --> 00:02:12.743
Featuring opens thirty days before an event starts, and it runs to the event's last day, or to the end of the season, whichever comes first.

00:02:12.743 --> 00:02:15.226
Tap See it, to open a covered event on the map.

00:02:17.415 --> 00:02:21.781
On the event, you see the Featured badge, and an Event Partner badge.

00:02:21.781 --> 00:02:25.396
The badge only shows that the organization has this plan.

00:02:25.396 --> 00:02:27.812
It is not an endorsement by SoCal Lights.

00:02:28.643 --> 00:02:31.899
Some founding cities have Event Partner free this year.

00:02:31.899 --> 00:02:36.614
Then the page says Founding partner, free through a date, and shows no price at all.

00:02:37.491 --> 00:02:39.211
That is Event Partner.

00:02:39.211 --> 00:02:44.801
Listing stays free, the plan is for events you want to feature, and the badge is not an endorsement.

00:02:46.174 --> 00:02:48.413
Next up: Feature your event or home.
